# Copy to .env. Put machine-specific overrides in .env.local.
# Settings: tutorial/07-running-the-rig.md#configuration

# ── LiveKit wire layer (required, all three peers) ──────────────────
LIVEKIT_URL=ws://localhost:7880
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=devkey
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=secret
LIVEKIT_ROOM=portal-hitl

# ── Hardware addresses ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Robot host. B601_PORT is the Damiao CAN adapter; cameras are one per
# video track in portal.yaml, named B601_CAM_<TRACK> with a trailing
# `_camera` dropped (arm_camera -> B601_CAM_ARM). Linux: /dev/videoN.
# macOS: an integer index. Find them with `v4l2-ctl --list-devices`.
B601_PORT=/dev/ttyACM0
B601_CAM_ARM=/dev/video0
# Only `arm_camera` is declared in portal.yaml. To add the overhead camera
# back, add its track there too -- setting this alone does nothing.
# B601_CAM_OVERHEAD=/dev/video2

# Operator host. Required there -- it has no default.
REBOT102_LEADER_PORT=/dev/ttyUSB0

# ── Arm safety (robot host) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The speed cap. The commanded target advances at most this many degrees
# per command, re-seeded from the arm's real pose at startup, after a bus
# rebuild, and whenever commands pause -- so a bus recovery, an operator
# handover and a cold start are all ramps, never lunges.
#
# It ramps the TARGET. It must never clamp the tracking error: this arm
# runs MIT impedance control, where torque is kp*(target - present), so
# capping that error caps the FORCE and the gravity-loaded joints stop
# moving altogether.
#
# It is per COMMAND, so the rate depends on PORTAL_FPS. At 30 fps:
#     0.17 ->   5 deg/s   (a 90 deg move takes 18s)
#     1.0  ->  30 deg/s   (3s)   <- bring-up, or an expensive workspace
#     5.0  -> 150 deg/s   (0.6s) <- the default
#     0    -> no cap at all
#
# The gripper is exempt (B601_UNCAPPED_JOINTS): it runs force_pos, not
# impedance control, so its force is already capped at 7% -- and 270 deg
# of travel at the arm's rate would make a grasp take two seconds.
# Listed here despite having a default: the right value depends on where
# the arm is and what it is near, which is a per-deployment decision.
B601_MAX_STEP_DEG=5.0

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Recorder host. Where each session's .rrd lands; defaults to
# `data/sessions`. The recorder needs the disk, so this is the one
# machine worth pointing somewhere with room.
# PORTAL_DATA_RRD_DIR=~/portal-sessions
